910; Hormisda papa, LXIII, 512; LXXXIV, 814; Victor
Carthagin., LXXXVII, 85; Elipandus, XCVI, 861, 870;
Amalarius, CV, 1333; Candidus, monachus Fuldensis,
CVI; Nicolaus I papa, CXIX, 855. — Quomodo Christus
est Messias praedictus, et quomodo venerit in tempore a
prophetis statuto, Alvarus Cordub., CXXI, 482, 485,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">seqq.,</HI>  495. — De Christo homine facto, Petrus Vener.,
CLXXXIX, 175; Gerhohus, CXCIII, 541, 552; Philippus
de Harveng, CCIII, 34; Alexander, Gemmeticensis abb.,
CCV, 919. — De meditanda Christi infantia et passione,
Adamus, abbas Perseniae, CCXI, 603.</P> <P COM="0113"><HI REND="ITALIC">De anima humana.</HI>  — De natura animae, Ambros., XVI,
1074. — De origine animae, Hieronym. et August.,
XXII, 1085, 1124, 1182; XXXIII, 585, 718, 720, 778,
857, 929. — De anima soluta corpore,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  77, 693,
