1190.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Veronica</HI>  beccabunga (pungo), S. Hildegardus, CXCVII,
1160.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vicia</HI>  dicta quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">vix</HI>  perveniat ad triplicem fructum,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 602. — Vicia faba, S. Hildegardis,
CXCVII, 1132. — Victa sativa (vichim),  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  1201.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vimen,</HI>  dictum quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">vim</HI>  habeat  <HI REND="ITALIC">multam</HI>  viroris, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 617. — De vimine, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 115.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vinea,</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 507; Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 163.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Viola</HI>  propter  <HI REND="ITALIC">vim odoris</HI>  nomen habet; hujus genera
sunt tria,  <HI REND="ITALIC">purpureum, album, melinum,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 626; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 528. — Viola purpurea,
humilis, odorifera, frigida, mollis, Hugo de S.
Victore, CLXXVII, 164. — De viola, S. Hildegardis,
CXCVII, 1170.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Virga.</HI>  — Quid sit virga, Hugo a S. Victore, CLXXVII,
112. — Virga quae deramis, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 607,
608. — Virga recta, gracilis, florem habet in summo,
flagellat et erudit, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 164.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Virgultum</HI>  ex  <HI REND="ITALIC">virga</HI>  appellatur quod ad radicem arboris
nascitur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 607; Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 111. — Quomodo ad vocem Domini subito
omne virgultorum genus efflorescens, victum, delicias ac
medicinam ministraverit, S. Ambrosius, XIV, 184.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Virgulum</HI>  est quod de radice pullulat, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 607.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Viriditas,</HI>  S. Ambrosius, XIV, 166; S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
608.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Virtus</HI>  seminaria, S. Ambrosius, XIV, 169.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Viticella</HI>  herba a Latinis appellata quod sicut  <HI REND="ITALIC">vitis</HI>  quidquid
proximum habuerit, apprehendat corymbis, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 634.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vitis</HI>  dicta quod vim habeat citius radicandi. Alii putant
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vites</HI>  dictas, quod invicem se  <HI REND="ITALIC">vittis</HI>  innectant, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 602  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seq.;</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 506. — De
vite, S. Ambrosius, XIV, 175, 185; S, Hildegardis,
CXCVII, 1244.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vulvus</HI>  appellatus quod radix ejus volubilis sit et
rotunda, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 633.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Weyt,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1205.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Wida,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1239.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Wichwurtz,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1196.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Wildelatich,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1165.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Wiszgras,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1164.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Wuntwurtz,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1146.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Xylicon</HI>  vel Latine siliqua, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 113.</P> <P COM="0544"><HI REND="ITALIC">Xyliglycon</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xuvlon glukuú</FOREIGN> ) arbor cujus pomo succus expressus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">acatia</HI>  a Graecis dicitur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 614;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 515.</P> <P COM="0544"><COL N="0545"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Xylobalsamum,</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 526.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Zizania,</HI>  quod poeta semper  <HI REND="ITALIC">infelix lolium</HI>  dicunt,
quod sit infecundum et inutile, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
635; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 529. — Lolium et zizania
 <COL N="0546"></COL> nunquam ex frumenti semine nascitur, S. Ambrosius,
XIV, 173.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Zucker,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1197.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Zugelnich,</HI>  S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1208.</P></DOC> <DOC NAME="Index agriculturae" AUTHOR="Editores" TEMPSTAT=MOD COM="0546" SECOND="NO"><COL N="0545"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0545">CCXXI.
INDEX AGRICULTURAE.
ALPHABETICE REVOCANS QUIDQUID DIXERE PATRES CIRCA SOLI CULTURAM
ET PRODUCTIONEM,
INSTRUMENTA RUSTICA, TEMPORA APTIORA, ETC., ETC.</HEAD> <DIV1 COM="0545" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0545">MONITUM.</HEAD> <P COM="0545">Agricultura late definiri potest: industria quae objectum habet culturam soli et productionem substantiarum
quae victui hominis nec non animalium domesticorum inserviunt. Agricultura est scientia in
quantum includit principia, et ars quoad methodorum applicationem. Ad exercendam agriculturam botanica
et zoologia multum proficiunt.</P> <P COM="0545">Index de Agricultura est quasi complementum INDICUM de BOTANICA et ZOOLOGIA.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0545" SECOND="NO"><HEAD TYPE=edit COM="0545">INDEX AGRICULTURAE.</HEAD> <P COM="0545"><COL N="0545"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Acetabulum</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">aceta ferum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
715.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Acetum</HI>  vel quia  <HI REND="ITALIC">acutum</HI>  vel quia  <HI REND="ITALIC">aquatum,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 712; Rabanus Maurus., CXI, 596.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aedificia rustica: casa, tugurium, tesqua, magalia,</HI> S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 552; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 409.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Afractum,</HI>  quod Latine spumeum vocatur, S. Isidor.,
LXXXII, 710.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Ager</HI>  Latine appellari dicitur eo quod in eo  <HI REND="ITALIC">agatur</HI>  aliquid.,
S. Isidor., LXXXII, 553; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 410. — Omnis
ager quadrifariam dividitur: aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">arvus</HI>  est
ager, aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">consitus,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">pascuus,</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">florens, ibid.</HI>  — Ager
a nocuis purgatur, stercoratur, multipliciter aratur, seminatur,
sepitur, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 135. — De
agris, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 553; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
410 — De finibus agrorum, de mensuris agrorum, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 554, 555; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 412.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Agrestes</HI>  artes docuerunt, Homogerus, Osiris, Triptolemus,
Ceres, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 597.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Agricola</HI>  mane consurgit, boves jugo sociat, tempora
arandi et seminandi observat, jactum semen patienter
exspectat, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 135.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Agricultura</HI>  plurimi delectantur, S. August., XXXIV,
1304. — Ejus encomium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  1304, 1305. — Agricultura
omnium artium innocentissima, id, XLII, 37. — In
usu esse coepit apud Graecos, regnante Argo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  564.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Alabastrum</HI>  vas unguentarium, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
718.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Alimonia</HI>  ab  <HI REND="ITALIC">alendo,</HI>  S. Isidor., LXXXII, 706, 707; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 587.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Amolum</HI>  flos farinae tenuissimum, prae levitate a mola
ejectum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 591.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Ampulla</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">ampla bulla,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 716;
Rabauus Maurus, CXI, 600.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Amystis</HI>  species peculi, S. Isidorus, 617; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 600.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Antella ante sellam,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 728.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Apicius</HI>  primus coquinae apparatum composuit, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 705; CXI, 587.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Apophoreta,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 715.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aratio</HI>  vernalis et autumnalis, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
598.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aratrum</HI>  ab  <HI REND="ITALIC">arando terram</HI>  vocatum, quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">araterrium,</HI> 
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 715; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 610. — Incertum
utrum specialiter vomere aut aratro terram
vertere instituit Ceres, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 597. — Arastrum
de ferro et ligno fit, terram findit, ab agricola tenetur,
terram meliorat, in campo dimittitur, Hugo S. de
Victore, CLXXXII, 137.</P> <P COM="0545"><HI REND="ITALIC">Arbores,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 606-623; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 508, 511. — Vide  <HI REND="ITALIC">Indicem Botanicae.</HI></P> <P COM="0545"><COL N="0546"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Arca</HI>  dicta quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">arceat</HI>  visum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
719; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 604.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Area</HI>  dicta a planitie atque aequalitate, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 554.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Areolae</HI>  concavo fiunt lapide, aquam ad hortum vehunt,
Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 137.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aretina</HI>  vasa ex Aretio dicta, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
715.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Assum</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">ardeat</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">arsum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 592.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Auctores</HI>  qui de rebus locuti sunt juxta S. Isidorum,
Hesiodus scilicet Booetius, Democritus, Cato, Marcus,
Tarentinus, Virgilius, Cornelius Celsus, Julius Atticus,
Aemilianus, Columella, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 597.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Axungia</HI>  ab unctione vocata, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Baccea</HI>  primum a Baccho, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 716;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 600.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Bacillus</HI>  a Baculo, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 724; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 609.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Baculus</HI>  a Baccho, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 724; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 609.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Basterna</HI>  vehiculum itineris quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">viae sternax,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 724.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Bestiae,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 433; Rabanus Maurus.
CXI, 217. — Vide  <HI REND="ITALIC">Indicem Zoologiae.</HI></P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Buris</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Boaúû oujrhú</FOREIGN> ) curvamentum aratri, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cacabus</HI>  et Cucuma a sono fervoris cognominantur, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 718; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 602.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Coelia</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">calefaciendo</HI>  est potio ex succo tritici per artem
confecta, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 713, 714.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Calamistrum,</HI>  acus ad intorquendos capillos, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Calcaria</HI>  dicta quia in calce hominis ligantur, S.
Isidorus. LXXXII, 728; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Candela a candendo</HI>  dicitur, quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">candendo deleatur,</HI> 
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 721; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
605.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Canicula</HI>  ferrens harpax, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 727.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Canistrum</HI>  fiscis canis contexitur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
719; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 604.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cantharus,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Capistrum</HI>  a capite jumentorum dictum, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 728; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Capsus</HI>  curruca undique contecta, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
724.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Capulum</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">capiendo,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 728; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Caracutium,</HI>  vehiculum altissimarum rotarum, quasi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">carrum acutum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 724.</P> <P COM="0546"><HI REND="ITALIC">Carnes</HI>  dictae quia charae sunt vel a creando, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 591.</P> <P COM="0546"><COL N="0547"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Carpentum</HI>  quasi carrum pompalicum, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 724; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 608.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Carrum</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">cardine</HI>  rotarum dictum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
723: Rebanus Maurus, CXI, 608.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Caseus</HI>  vocatur quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">careat sero</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">careum,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 710; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 593.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Catenatum</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">capiendo teneat,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
725; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 610.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Catinum</HI>  vas fictile, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717; Rabanus,
Maurus, CXI, 601.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cauterium</HI>  dictum quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">cauturium</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">urat,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 728; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 613.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cervisia</HI>  a Cerere, id est, fruge vocata, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 713.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Chamus,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 727.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Character,</HI>  ferrum coloratum quo notae pecudibus inuruntur,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 728; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 613.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cibus</HI>  quia capitur ore, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 706; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 587.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cibutum</HI>  Graecum nomen est quod nos dicimus aream,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 719.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cinis</HI>  est incendium per quod aeger inutilem humorem
exsudat, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 598.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cistella</HI>  a costis ex canna vel ligno, quibus contexitur
nominata, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 720.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Clavis</HI>  quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">claudat,</HI>  S. Isodorus, LXXXII, 725; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 610.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cochlear,</HI>  ab usu prius cochlearum dictum, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 715.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Coctum</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">coactum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 592.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Caena</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>koinoún</FOREIGN>  commune) est vespertinus cibus, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 708; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 589.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Colostrum</HI>  lac novum quod neutri generis est, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 710.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Conditum,</HI>  commistione pigmentorum compositum,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 712, 713.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cophinus</HI>  est vas ex virgultis contextum, aptum mundare
stercora, et terram portare, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
720; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 604.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Coquinae</HI>  apparatum Apicius primus composuit, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 705; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 587.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Corbes</HI>  dictae quia curvatis virgis contexuntur, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 720.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cratera</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú touð krateiðn</FOREIGN> ) calix est duas habens ansas,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 716; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 599.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cribrum</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">currifrugum,</HI>  quod ibi currat frumentum,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 719; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
603. — Cribrum purum ab impuro separat, grossa retinet,
minuta expellit, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII,
143.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Crudum</HI>  quod sit cruentum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 592.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Crusta</HI>  est superficies panis, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 708;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 591.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cultelli</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">cultura</HI>  dicti, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 725; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 611. — Cultellus manubrio tenetur,
ferro incidit, vagina custoditur, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 143.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cultura</HI>  agrorum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 597, 598; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 503. — Cultura plantarum, Walafrid.
Strabus, CXIV, 1122.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cupos</HI>  et cupas a  <HI REND="ITALIC">capiendo,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 601.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Currus</HI>  quatuor rotis volvitur; quanto plus oneratur,
tanto plus stridet, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 143.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cyathi</HI>  quoque et scyphi poculorum sunt genera, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 716; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 608.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cylindrus</HI>  lapis est teres in modum columnae, S, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 726.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Cymbia</HI>  poculorum genus, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 715;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 600.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Dentale</HI>  est aratri pars prima quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">deus,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Digitus</HI>  est pars minima mensurarum agrestium, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 555.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Discus</HI>  antea  <HI REND="ITALIC">iscus</HI>  vocabatur a specie  <HI REND="ITALIC">scuti,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 715; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 598.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Dolium,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 601. — Dolium rotundum, circulatum, intextum,
profundum, patulum, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXXII, 143.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Domus</HI>  quomodo aedificata, S. Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 144.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Dulcia</HI>  sunt genera pistorii operis a sapore dicta, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 708; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 591.</P> <P COM="0547"><HI REND="ITALIC">Elixum</HI>  quod in aqua sola decoquitur, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 592.</P> <P COM="0547"><COL N="0548"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Esca,</HI>  quia eam os capit, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 706; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 587. — De escis, S: Isidorus, LXXXII,
705-711; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 587-594.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Faecula,</HI>  uva pinguis, decocta usque ad crassitudinem,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 713.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Faex</HI>  dicta quod sese vasis emergendo affigat, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 711.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Falcastrum,</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">falcis</HI>  similitudine vocatum, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 611.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Falx</HI>  est qua arbores putantur et vites, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 411. — Falx acuta
est, recurva, propius tondet, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 146.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Farcimen</HI>  caro concisa et minuta, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
710.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Farina</HI>  et furfures a  <HI REND="ITALIC">farre</HI>  dictae cujus sunt purgamenta,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
591. — Farina minuta est, munda est, cum labore habetur,
per aquam conglutinatur, fermentatur, acedinem sumit,
Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 146.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Favus</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fageiðn</FOREIGN> , S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 711; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 594.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fermentum</HI>  a fervore nuncupatum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 597. — Fermentum modicum
farinae conglutinatae immittitur, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 146.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fictilia,</HI>  quod fiant et fingantur ex terra, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 714; Rabanus Maurus., CXI, 594. — Fictilia vasa
in Samo insula prius inventa traduntur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI></P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fimus</HI>  dispersus terram fecundat, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 146.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fines,</HI>  dicti eo quod agri funiculis sunt divisi, S. Isidorus.,
LXXXII, 554; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 411.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fisclum,</HI>  quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">fisculum,</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">calando</HI>  oleum dictum, S.
Isidorus., LXXXII, 726.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Focus</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fwðû</FOREIGN> ), ignis, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 720; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 605.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fomes</HI>  hastulae species, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 608.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Forfices,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 724; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 610.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fossio,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 606; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 597.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fossorium,</HI>  quod foveat, quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">fovessorium,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 726.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Frena,</HI>  quod equos fremere cogant, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
727; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Frixum</HI>  a sono dictum quando in oleo ardet, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 709; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 592.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Frumentum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 600, 601; Rabanus
Maurus., CXI, 505. — Vid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Indicem Butaniae.</HI></P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Frustum</HI>  vocatum quod capiatur a  <HI REND="ITALIC">frumine,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 710; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 591.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Furcillae</HI>  dictae eo quod iis frumenta cilluntur, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 726.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fustes,</HI>  quod praefixi in terris  <HI REND="ITALIC">stent,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
724.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Germen.</HI>  Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 112.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Girgillus,</HI>  quod in gyrum vertatur, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 727.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Glans,</HI>  cibus porcorum est, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 148.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Granum</HI>  seritur, moritur, Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII,
148.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Habenae</HI>  ab  <HI REND="ITALIC">habendo</HI>  dictae, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 728.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hastula,</HI>  a  <HI REND="ITALIC">tollendo</HI>  nuncupata, quasi  <HI REND="ITALIC">abstula,</HI>  S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 608.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Haustra,</HI>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">rota</HI>  ab hauriendo dicta, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 726; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 726.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hemicadium,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 713.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Herbae</HI>  aromaticae, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 527. — Vide
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Indicem Botanicae.</HI></P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hordeum,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 600; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 505.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hortus</HI>  nominatur quod semper ibi aliquid  <HI REND="ITALIC">oriatur,</HI>  S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 635; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 530. — Hortus
circumfoditur et circumsepitur arborum distinctione
ornatus, floribus jucundus, Hugo de S. Victore,
CLXXVII, 154.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Horologium</HI>  quod ibi horas legamus, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 725; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 610.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hydria</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uådwr</FOREIGN> ). S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717; Rabanus
Maurus, 600.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hydromelum,</HI>  quod fiat ex aqua et malis Matianis, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 713.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Impositio oculorum,</HI>  cum inciso cortice libro alienae
arboris germen immittitur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 607.</P> <P COM="0548"><HI REND="ITALIC">Insitio</HI>  dicitur, cum fisso trunco surculus fecundae arboris
sterili inseritur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 607.</P> <P COM="0548"><COL N="0549"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Intermissio</HI>  est qua alternis annis ager vacuus vires
recipit, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 598.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta</HI>  equorum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 727; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta</HI>  hortorum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 726; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta</HI>  rustica, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 705-725;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 610.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Itinera,</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 412.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Jentaculum</HI>  primus cibus quo jejunium solvitur, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 707.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Jugum</HI>  duos conjungit, ad terram premit, capiti colligatur,
Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 149.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Jumenta,</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 199. — Jumentum in
fimo suo versatur et quiescit, vilibus pascitur, ossiferum
est, sessores non discernit. Hugo de S. Victore, CLXXVII,
149.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Labrum, labellum</HI>  eo quod in eo solent infantes lavari,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 601.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lac</HI>  ( <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>leukoún</FOREIGN> ) a Graeco sermone derivatum est pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">candore,</HI> 
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 710. — Lac album est, parvulos
nutrit, coagulatum arescit, bulliendo elevatur, Hugo
de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 150.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lactatum</HI>  est potio  <HI REND="ITALIC">a lacte;</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 713.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lacus</HI>  quo liquatum profluit, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 726;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 612.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Laganum</HI>  est latus et tenuis panis qui primum in aqua,
postea in oleo frigitur, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 708.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lagena,</HI>  S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 717; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 600.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Laguncula</HI>  ex pluribus asseribus est texta, circulis ferreis
constricta, spiraculum habet, vinum conservat, Hugo
de S. Victore, CLXXVII, 150.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lardum</HI>  eo quod in domo repositum conservatur; nam
antiqui domos  <HI REND="ITALIC">lares</HI>  dicebant, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 709.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Laterna</HI>  quod lucem interius habeat, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 721; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 606.</P> <P COM="0549"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lebetes</HI>  aenei sunt Graeco nomine vocati, S. Isidorus,
