mensura minima omnium agrestium mensurarum,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 555; Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 96.</P> <P COM="0579">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gradus.</HI>  — Gradus quid in superficie, Sylvester II,
CXXXIX, 98.</P> <P COM="0579">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Juchus.</HI>  — De jucho, quadam agrorum mensura, fit
mentio, Notkerus, CXXXI, 168.</P> <P COM="0579">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jugerum.</HI>  — Jugerum, quaenam mensura, Hieronymus,
XXIV, 80, 81; Boetius, LXIII, 1358; S. Isidorus,
 <COL N="0580"></COL> LXXXII, 556; Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 97. — Jugeri etymologia,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI></P> <P COM="0580">11. —  <HI REND="ITALIC">Laterculus.</HI>  — Laterculi superficies et etymologia,
Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 97.</P> <P COM="0580">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Leuca.</HI>  — Leuca quid in superficie constrata, Sylvester
II, CXXXIX, 98.</P> <P COM="0580">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Palmus.</HI>  — Palmi definitur superficies, Boetius,
LXIII, 1352; Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 99.</P> <P COM="0580">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Passus.</HI>  — Passus quid in superficie constratus,
S. Isidorus, LXXVII, 556.</P> <P COM="0580">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pertica.</HI>  — Quot perticas habet passus, Sylvester II,
CXXXIX, 98.</P> <P COM="0580">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pes.</HI>  — Quid intelligitur per pedem contractum,
Boetius, LXIII, 1336. — Pedis contracti definitur superficies,
Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 99.</P> <P COM="0580">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Porta.</HI>  — Portae quaenam superficies, Sylvester II,
CXXXIX, 97.</P> <P COM="0580">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Scamnum.</HI>  — Scamnum mensura veterum agrimensorum,
Boetius, LXIII, 1335. — Scamnum agrorum
mensura longior,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  1354.</P> <P COM="0580">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sexta.</HI>  — Sextae superficies, Sylvester II, CXXXIX,
96, 99.</P> <P COM="0580">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Striga.</HI>  Quid est striga, Lactantius, VII, 449. — In
quo striga a scamno distinguitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  707. — Striga
agrorum mensura, Boetius, LXIII, 1354.</P> <P COM="0580">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tabula.</HI>  — Tabula quarta pars jugeri, Sylvester II,
CXXXIX, 97.</P> <P COM="0580">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Uncia.</HI>  — Uncia quid in superficie constrata, Sylvester
II, CXXXIX, 99.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0580" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0580">IV. —  <HI REND="ITALIC">De mensuris capacitatis.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0580">Quid per solidum intelligitur, Boetius, LXIII, 1337;
Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 95. — Sequuntur variae capacitatis
mensurae.</P> <P COM="0580">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Acetabulum.</HI>  — Acetabuli capacitas, Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0580">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Amphora.</HI>  — Chilperici statutum de amphora, S.
Gregorius Turonensis, LXXI, 346. — Amphorae notatur
capacitas, S. Gregorius Magnus, LXXVII, 499 not.;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488, 489. — De urna et amphora
fit mentio, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 593; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0580">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Artaba.</HI>  — Artabae vario modo definitur capacitas,
S. Hieronymus, XXIV, 81; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 596;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488.</P> <P COM="0580">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Batus.</HI>  — Batus mensura Hebraica, S. Hieronymus,
XXIX, 80; Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1026. — Exprimitur
bati capacitas, S. Hieronymus, XXIV, 81; XXV, 450; S.
Isidorus, LXXXI, 595; Rabanus Maurus, CIX, 176; CXI,
488. — Batus mensura liquidorum, S. Hieronymus,
XXIV, 81; Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1026. — Bati etymologia,
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488.</P> <P COM="0580">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bilibris.</HI>  — Bilibris quid, Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
486; Rupertus, CLXIX, 944. — De bilibri loquitur Apocalypsis,
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0580">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cadus.</HI>  — Cadus in Evangelio, Eugyppius, LXII,
841; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 489 — Cadi capacitas, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 595; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488.</P> <P COM="0580">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Choenix.</HI>  — Choenix cujusnam capacitatis, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 594; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0580">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Choncula.</HI>  — Notatur capacitas chonculae, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 593.</P> <P COM="0580">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cochlear.</HI>  — Cochlear mensurarum pars minima, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 593.</P> <P COM="0580">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Congius.</HI>  — Congius mensura liquidorum et aridorum,
Cassianus, XLIX, 1135 not.; S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
594; Anastasius, CXXXVIII, 666 not. — Congii praefixa
capacitas, Cassianus, XLIX, 1135 not.; S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 594; Anastasius, CXXXVIII, 666 not.</P> <P COM="0580">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Corus.</HI>  — Corus cujusnam capacitatis, S. Hieronymus,
XXV, 450; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 596, 760, 841;
Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1026; CXI, 488.</P> <P COM="0580">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cotula.</HI>  — Cotula quaenam capacitatis mensura, S.
Hieronymus, XXV, 450; Cassianus, XLIX, 1135 not.; S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 760; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0580">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cubus.</HI>  — Cubus amphorae capacitatem habet,
Arnobius, V, 695.</P> <P COM="0580">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cyathus.</HI>  — Cyathus quid, Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
486.</P> <P COM="0580">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ephi.</HI>  — Ephi definitur capacitas, S. Hieronymus,
XXIV, 81; Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1026. — Ephi mensura
Hebraica, S. Hieronymus, XXV, 459; Rabanus Maurus,
CX, 1026. — Ephi mensura aridorum. Rabanus Maurus,
CX, 1026; CXI, 488. — Ephi imago Trinitatis, Walafridus,
CXXX, 313. — Ephi et Batus eadem mensura, Rupertus,
CLXVII, 666.</P> <P COM="0580">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Galeta.</HI>  — De galetae mensura mentio facta, Ven.
Guibertus, CLVI, 1155, 1156.</P> <P COM="0580">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gomor.</HI>  — Gomor cujusnam sit capacitatis, S. Hieronymus,
 <COL N="0581"></COL> XXV, 450; S. Isidorus, LXXXI, 594, 596, 760;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488; Rupertus, CLXVII, 666.</P> <P COM="0581">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hemina.</HI>  — Heminae praefixa capacitas, Cassianus,
XLIX, 1136 not.; S. Benedictus, LXVI, 643; Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 486. — Capacitas heminae juxta varias
sententias, S. Benedictus, LXVI, 644.</P> <P COM="0581">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Justa.</HI>  — Justa mensura solita vini, Ven. Guibertus,
CLVI, 1066.</P> <P COM="0581">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Medimna.</HI>  — Medimna quinque modiorum mensura,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 595, 596; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 488; Anastasius, CXXVII, 1544. — Medimnae in
Evangelio mentio facta,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI></P> <P COM="0581">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Metreta.</HI>  — Metretae etymologia, S. Augustinus,
XXXV, 1461. — Metreta et amphora,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  Arator.,
LXVIII, 224 not. — Metreta mensura liquidorum, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 594; Anastasius, CXXVII, 1544.</P> <P COM="0581">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Modius.</HI>  — Modii notatur capacitas, S. Gregorius
Magnus, LXXVII, 499 not.; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 595;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 487, 488; Anastasius, CXXVIII,
666 not. — De modio in Scriptura sacra, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 595, 666; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 487, 488;
Walafridus, CXIII, 313. — Modii etymologia, Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 487.</P> <P COM="0581">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omer.</HI>  — Omer mensura Hebraica, S. Hieronymus,
XXIV, 80, 81.</P> <P COM="0581">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quartarius.</HI>  — Miraculum de vasculo quartarium
non tenente, S. Gregorius Turonensis, LXXI, 710.</P> <P COM="0581">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pinta.</HI>  — De pinta Dionysiana, S. Benedictus,
LXVI, 613.</P> <P COM="0581">26  <HI REND="ITALIC">Satum.</HI>  — Satum mensura Palaestinae, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 595. — Sati capacitas, Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
488. — De sato evangelico,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI></P> <P COM="0581">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sextarius.</HI>  — Sextarius cujusnam sit capacitatis,
Cassianus, XLIX, 1135; S. Gregorius Magnus. LXXVII,
599 not.; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 594; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0581">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Urna.</HI>  — Urna et amphora mensurae sunt, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 594. — Urna idem ac quartarius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
595. — Urnae capacitas, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 488.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0581" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0581">V. —  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pondera.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0581">Ponderis definitio, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 590. — Explicantur
variae staterae partes,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  590, 591. — Cunctis
corporibus est pondus, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 479, 481. — Phidon
argivus ponderum constitutor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  479. — Sequuntur
variae ponderis mensurae.</P> <P COM="0581">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">As.</HI>  — As in duodecim partes dividitur, D. Ausonius,
XIX, 908; S. Gregorius Magnus, LXXVII, 1010 not.;
Ven. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 675.</P> <P COM="0581">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bace.</HI>  — Bace Hebraicum pondus, S. Hieronymus,
XXIII, 973.</P> <P COM="0581">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bessis.</HI>  — Bessis pondus definitur, D. Ausonius,
XIX, 909; Ven. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
675.</P> <P COM="0581">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Centenarium.</HI>  — Centenariii pondus et etymologia,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 591; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481.</P> <P COM="0581">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ceratum.</HI>  — Ceratum cujusnam ponderis, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 591; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481.</P> <P COM="0581">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Chalcus.</HI>  — Chalco quodnam pondus, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 591. — Chalco quaenam etymologia, Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 481.</P> <P COM="0581">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Choncula.</HI>  — Choncula drachma una et dimidia impletur,
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0581">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Decunx, deunx, dextans, dodrans.</HI>  — Quid sint indicatur,
D. Ausonius, XIX, 909; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
675.</P> <P COM="0581">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Drachma.</HI>  — Drachma octava pars unciae, S. Hieronymus,
XXV, 48; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 591.</P> <P COM="0581">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Duella.</HI>  — Duellae pondus, Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
482. — Duella per quodnam signum exprimatur, Sylvester
II, CXXXIX, 100 not.</P> <P COM="0581">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Granum.</HI>  — Exprimitur grani pondus, S. Gregorius
Magnus, LXXVII, 700 not.</P> <P COM="0581">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Libra.</HI>  — Libra quid et quotuplex, Cassianus,
XLIX, 211 not.; S. Benedictus, LXVI, 627; S. Gregorius
Magnus, LXXVII, 499 not., 539 not.; S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
592. — Librae etymologia, Cassianus, XLIX, 212 not.</P> <P COM="0581">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Marca.</HI>  — De marca fit mentio, Albericus, CLXVI,
464; Willelmus Remensis, CCIX, 826.</P> <P COM="0581">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mina.</HI>  — Minae pondus, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 593;
Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1026. — Mina Graecum nomen, id.,
CXI, 483.</P> <P COM="0581">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obolus.</HI>  — Recensentur obolus et semi obolus,
Boetius, LXIII, 1352. — Oboli pondus, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 591; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481. — Oboli
signum, Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 100 not.</P> <P COM="0581">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Oxybaphus.</HI>  — Oxybaphus cujusnam ponderis,
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0581"><COL N="0582"></COL> 17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quadrans.</HI>  — Quadrans apud Hebraeos, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 592. — De quadrantis pondere, Ven. Beda, XC,
307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 675.</P> <P COM="0582">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quincunx.</HI>  — Quincunx cujusnam sit ponderis,
Ven. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 675.</P> <P COM="0582">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Scripulus.</HI>  — Scripuli aestimatur pondus, S. Isidorus,
LXXII, 591; Ven. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus,
CVII, 675; CXI, 481. — Scripulus unde nomen sumpsit,
id., CVII, 675.</P> <P COM="0582">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Semis, senarium, sexcunx, sextans, sextula, sicilicus.</HI>  — Cujusnam
sint ponderis, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 515;
Ven. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 482, 675.</P> <P COM="0582">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siclus.</HI>  — Siclus ex Hebraica voce nomen sumpsit,
S. Hieronymus, XXIII, 973. — Siclus idem ac stater, id.,
XXV, 48. — Refertur sicli pondus apud varios populos,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 592; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 482.</P> <P COM="0582">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siliqua.</HI>  — Siliqua sexta pars scripuli, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 591; V. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
675, CXI, 481.</P> <P COM="0582">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stater.</HI>  — Stateris refertur pondus, S. Augustinus,
XXXVII, 1783; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 482. — De
statere loquitur Apocalypsis, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 486.</P> <P COM="0582">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Triens.</HI>  — Triens quatuor unciis par est, Ven.
Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 675.</P> <P COM="0582">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Uncia.</HI>  — Unciae etymologia, Cassianus, XLIX,
212. — Unciae pondus exprimitur, Cassianus, XLIX, 212
not; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 592; V. Beda, XC, 307; Rabanus
Maurus, CVII, 675 et CXI, 482. — Uncia duodecima
pars librae, Cassianus, XCIX, 212 not.; S. Benedictus, LXVI,
649; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 592. — Uncia per quodnam
exprimatur signum, Silvester II, CXXXIX, 100 not.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0582" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0582">VI. —  <HI REND="ITALIC">Monetae.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0582">De aedificiis in quo cudebantur nummi, Lactantius, VII,
205 not.; Carolus Magnus, XCVII, 553. — De monetae
adulterae fabricatoribus, S. Hieronymus, XXIII, 20; Carolus
Magnus, XCVII, 321, 322; Regino Prumiensis, CXXXII,
448. — Monetarum effigies, Marius Mercator, XLVIII,
154 not.; Prudentius, LX, 61; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 585. — Monetae
integritatis utilitas, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 725. — Proportio
argenti ad aurum in variis temporibus et
populis, S. Gregorius Magnus, LXXXVII, 630, 631 not. — Monetae
etymologia, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 585. — Numisma
ex quibus coalescit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  585. — De antiquissima
moneta, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 483. — Quid aerarium, thesaurus,
tributum, vectigal,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  483, 484. — Argenti,
auri et aeris variae species,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  485. — Sequuntur variae
monetae.</P> <P COM="0582">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Argentei.</HI>  — De triginta argenteis proditionis pretio
Juda traditis, Rupertus, CLXIX, 944; Petrus Comestor,
CXCVIII, 1614.</P> <P COM="0582">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">As.</HI>  — Decima pars denarii, S. Augustinus, XL, 38.</P> <P COM="0582">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aureus.</HI>  — Aurei coronati quoddam numisma, Lactantius,
VI, 276 not. — Aureorum pretium, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 592.</P> <P COM="0582">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Denarius.</HI>  — Denarius evangelicus, S. Augustinus,
XL, 410; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481. — Definitur denarii
pretium, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 315; S. Gregorius
Magnus, LXXVII, 631 not. — Denarii etymologia, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 591. — Post quoddam tempus denarius
vilescit, Carolus Magnus, XCVII, 136. — Non negandi
boni denarii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  576.</P> <P COM="0582">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Doppia.</HI>  — Doppia moneta Hispanica, Anastasius,
CXXVII, 1593.</P> <P COM="0582">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Drachma, Didrachma.</HI>  — De drachma evangelica, S.
Hieronymus, XXIII, 328; Marius Mercator, XLVIII, 154;
S. Gregorius Magnus, LXXVI, 1249; Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 481. — Didrachma duplex drachma, S. Augustinus,
XXXVII, 1783; S. Paschasius, CXX, 599. — Didrachma
cujusnam pretii, Christianus Druthmarus, CVI,
1406. — Drachmae notatur pretium, Rabanus Maurus,
CXI, 481. — Quid drachma, ae; et quid drachma, atis,
Petrus Comestor, CXCVIII, 1584.</P> <P COM="0582">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Follis.</HI>  — Follis etymologia. S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
585.</P> <P COM="0582">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Julius</HI>  — Julii pretium, Anastasius, CXXVIII, 666. — Julius
idem ac denarius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI></P> <P COM="0582">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Libra.</HI>  — Cujusnam sit pretii, Theodosius Magnus,
XIII, 492 not.; Rupertus, CLXIX, 944.</P> <P COM="0582">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Minutum.</HI>  — Minutum dimidia pars quadrantis, S.
Hieronymus, XXV, 38.</P> <P COM="0582">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nummus.</HI>  — Per nummos intelliguntur denarii,
Arator, LXVIII, 212 not. — Nummorum origo et etymologia,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 585; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
485.</P> <P COM="0582">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obolus.</HI>  — Nominatur obolus, Vita Patrum, LXXIII,
1220. — Oboli pretium, Rabanus Maurus, CX, 1027</P> <P COM="0582">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quadrans.</HI>  — Quadrantis notatur pretium, S. Hieronymus,
 <COL N="0583"></COL> XXVI, 38. — De quadrante evangelico, S.
Paschasius, CXX, 246, 247.</P> <P COM="0583">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sestertius.</HI>  — Sestertius quarta pars denarii, S.
Gregorius Magnus, LXXVII, 499 not.</P> <P COM="0583">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siclus.</HI>  — Sicli pretium, S. Hieronymus, XXV, 48;
Rabanus Maurus, CVIII, 288; CX, 1026.</P> <P COM="0583">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siliqua.</HI>  — Siliqua cujusnam sit pretii, S. Gregorius
Magnus, LXXVII, 630; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 591;
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481. — Signum quo siliqua exprimitur,
Sylvester II, CXXXIX, 100 not.</P> <P COM="0583">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Solidus.</HI>  — Solidus aureum numisma, Constantinus
Magnus, VIII, 344. — Varia documenta de pretio solidi,
S. Gregorius Magnus, LXXVII, 539, 630, 631, 799 not.;
LXXVIII, 459; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 592; Anastasius,
CXXVII, 1593; CXXVIII, 666 not. — Solidi etymologia,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 592; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 81;
Anastasius, CXXVIII, 666 not. — Solidi origo, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 592; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 481, 482. — Solidi
expressa imago ex nummis veteribus deprompta,
Anastasius, CXXVIII, 667.</P> <P COM="0583">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stater.</HI>  — Stater cujusnam pretii, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 592; Christianus Druthmarus, CVI, 1406; S.
Paschasius, CXX, 600. — De statere evangelico, S. Paschasius,
CXX, 600 et 601.</P> <P COM="0583">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Talentum</HI>  De talento evangelico, S. Gregorius Magnus,
LXXIII, 1108  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.</HI>  — Nihil talento majus, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 593; Walafridus, CXIII, 658; S. Anselmus,
CLVIII, 619. — Talenti pretium, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 593; Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 483. — Talentum
triplex, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 593; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
483.</P> <P COM="0583">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tartaron.</HI>  — Tartaron moneta Byzantina, Albericus,
CLXVI, 400, 420.</P> <P COM="0583">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tremissis.</HI>  — Tremissis cujusnam sit pretii, S.
Gregorius Magnus, LXXVII, 700 not.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0583" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0583">VII. —  <HI REND="ITALIC">Temporis mensurae.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0583">De variis modis tempus computandi, S. Hieronymus,
XXIV, 392; Sidonius Apollinaris, LVIII, 484 not. S.
Gregorius Magnus, LXXVIII, 477; Ven. Beda, XC, 953;
954; Claudius Taurin., CIV, 797; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
676, 678; Wandalbertus, CXXI, 631, 633; Hermanus,
CXLIII, 405  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.,</HI>  409 et 410. — Temporis definitiones,
S. Isidorus, LXXXIII, 974; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
676. — Temporis etymologia, Ven. Beda, XC, 579;
Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 678. — De variis divisionibus
temporis, Ven. Beda, XC, 579; Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
677. — Aevum quid, Honorius Augustodunensis, CLXXII,
145. — Sequuntur variae temporis mensurae.</P> <P COM="0583">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Annus.</HI>  — De anni computationibus apud Aegyptios,
Lactantius, VI, 325 not. — Anni definitiones, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 222; LXXXIII, 971; CXXIX, 1295, 1296. — Anni
etymologia, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 222; Ven. Beda, XC,
589. — Variae annorum species, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 249;
Ven. Beda, XC, 284; Helpericus, CXXXVII, 21. — De
anno dissertationes, S. Isidorus, LXXXIII, 971  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.</HI></P> <P COM="0583">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Atomus.</HI>  — Atomi duratio, Ven. Beda, XC, 302
not.; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 677; CXXIX, 1316. — Atomi
exiguilas, Ven. Beda, XC, 305, 580; Honorius Augusto
lunensis, CLXXII, 147.</P> <P COM="0583">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dies.</HI>  — Dissertatio de tribus diebus sepulturae
Christi, Lactantius, VII, 194 not. — Dierum nomina, D.
Ansonius, XIX, 910; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 217; LXXXIII,
967; Ven. Beda, XC, 583; Honorius Augustodunensis,
CLXXII, 150; Petrus Cantor, CCV, 419. — De diebus considerationes
variae, S. Augustinus, XXXIX, 193; Ven. Beda,
XC, 309  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.;</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 679, 680. — Diei
species, S. Bened. LXVI, 411 et 413; S. Isidorus,
 <COL N="0584"></COL> LXXXII 215. — Varium apud varios populos diei initium,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 215; Ven. Beda, XC, 279, 280. — Diei
etymologia, Ven. Beda, XC, 307 not. — Diei duratio,
id., XC, 309  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.</HI></P> <P COM="0584">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hora.</HI>  — Variae diei horae, S. Hieronymus, XXVI,
141. — Horae olim inaequales, Sidonius Apollinaris,
LVIII, 485. — Horae etymologia, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
215; Ven. Beda, XC, 580; Honorius Augustodunensis,
CLXXII, 147. — Horae quaenam sit duratio, Ven.
Beda, XC, 302; CXXIX, 1316; Honorius Augustodunensis,
CLXVI, 147.</P> <P COM="0584">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hebdomada.</HI>  — Hebdomadae primitiva constitutio,
S Victor, V, 305. — Hebdomadae etymologia, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 218 et 219. — Quot in hebdomada dies,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
968; Ven. Beda, XC, 281. — De septuaginta hebdomadis
propheticis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  333. — Variae hebdomadarum species,
Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 296  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.</HI></P> <P COM="0584">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lustrum.</HI>  — Lustrum inter varias temporis divisiones,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 208.</P> <P COM="0584">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mensis.</HI>  — Exponuntur duodecim menses, XIII, 463. — Menses
unde supputantur, S. Hieronymus, XXV, 286. — Mensis
etymologia, S. Hieronymus, XXV, 286; Ven.
Beda, XC, 341. — Mensium nomina, S. Prosper Aquitanus,
LI, 548, 556, 564; S. Isidorus, LXXXIII, 969. — De
mensium signis, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 184. — Mensis
definitio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  968; CXXIX, 1302. — Mensis vitae hominis
imago,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  969. — De mensibus apud varias gentes,
S. Isidorus, LXXXIII, 970; Ven. Beda, XC, 281,
282, 341  <HI REND="ITALIC">et seqq.;</HI>  CXXIX, 1302, 1303; Honorius Augustodunensis,
CLXXII, 152. — De concordia mensium, S.
Isidorus, LXXXIII, 974. — Horae variae quibus incipiunt.
singuli menses, Ven. Beda, XC, 358 not.</P> <P COM="0584">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Minutum.</HI>  — Minuti duratio, Ven. Beda, XC, 302
not., 580; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 678; CXXIX, 1293; Honorius
Augustodunensis, CLXXII, 147. — Minuti etymologia,
Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 678; CXXIX, 1293.</P> <P COM="0584">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Momentum.</HI>  — Momentum quid, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
208, 211; Ven. Beda, XC, 278; Alcuinus, CI, 1113. — Momentum
quodnam sit tempus, Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
677; CXXIX, 1293, 1318. — Momenti etymologia, CXXIX,
1293.</P> <P COM="0584">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Olympias.</HI>  — Humana auctoritate tempus in Olympiadas
divisum fuit, Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 676.</P> <P COM="0584">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ostensum.</HI>  — Ostensum minima temporis divisio,
Ven. Beda, XC, 303. — Ostensi duratio, Rabanus Maurus,
CVII. 677. — Ostensi etymologia, Honorius Augustodunensis,
CLXXII, 147.</P> <P COM="0584">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pars.</HI>  — Partis etymologia, Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
678. — Pars quodnam sit tempus, Rabanus Maurus, CVII,
678; Honorius Augustodunensis, CLXXII, 147.</P> <P COM="0584">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Punctum.</HI>  — Puncti duratio quaenam, Ven. Beda,
XC, 302 not., 303; CXXIX, 1292, 1317. — Puncti etymologia,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  XC, 580; CXXIX, 1293.</P> <P COM="0584">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quadrans.</HI>  — Quadrantis duratio varie aestimatur,
Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 678; CXXIX, 1293, 1319. — Quadrantis
etymologia, CXXIX, 1319.</P> <P COM="0584">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saeculum.</HI>  — Saecula temporibus structa, Tertull.,
II, 483. — Saeculi variae interpretationes, S. Hilarius, IX,
577; Ven. Beda, XC, 278, 279; Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
306; Honorius Augustodunensis, CLXXII, 157. — Saeculi
etymologia, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 233.</P> <P COM="0584">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Uncia.</HI>  — Uncia quaedam antiqua temporis mensura,
Ven. Beda, XC, 307.</P> <P COM="0584">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vicissitudo.</HI>  — Quatuor in anno vicissitudines, D.
Ausonius, XIX, 911; Rabanus Maurus, CVII, 687; CXI,
307. — Vicissitudines ex tribus mensibus coalescunt, Honorius
Augustodunensis, CLXXII, 153 et 154.</P></DIV1></DOC> <DOC NAME="Index archaeologiae" AUTHOR="Editores" TEMPSTAT=MOD COM="0584" SECOND="NO"><COL N="0583"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0583">CCXXVI.
INDEX ARCHAEOLOGIAE
EXHIBENS SCILICET ALPHABETICE QUIDQUID SCRIPSERE PATRES CIRCA
ARCHITECTURAM, SCULPTURAM, PICTURAM, ETC.</HEAD> <DIV1 COM="0583" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0583"><HI REND="ITALIC">Abbatiae seu monasteria.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0583">De restauratione monasterii Centulensis, S. Angilbertus,
abbas S. Richarii Centulensis, XCIX, 841, 842. — Incendium
Tuitii, B. Rupertus, abbas Tuitiensis, CLXX,
 <COL N="0584"></COL> 332-334. — De combustione monasterii Gemblacensis,
Guibertus Gemblacensis abbas, CLX, 657.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0584" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0584"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aedes civiles.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0584">Descriptio urbis Romae, Publius Victor, XVIII, 437-438. — Obelisci,
 <COL N="0585"></COL> XVIII., 449, 450. — Pontes, fora, basilicae,
thermae, aquae, etc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  451-453; Victor Vitensis,
LVIII, 184. — Columnae marmoreae et lapides ad urbem
Ravennam devehendae, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 581. — Horrea
publica reaedificanda,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  592. — Cloacae reparandae,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  592, 760. — Trabes devehendae ad Alsuanum,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  616. — Quadrati lapides Ravennam devehendae,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  651. — Moenia, munia, murus, turres, propugnacula,
promurale, porta, plateae, quintana, cloacae, imboli, S.
Isidorus, LXXXII, 538. — Forus, curia, praetorium, gymnasia,
capitolium, arces, circum, theatrum, amphitheatrum,
labyrinthus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  539. — Pharus, cochleae, thermae,
balnea, apodyterium, popina, tabernae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  540. — Macellum,
mercatum, telonium, carcer,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  541. — Habitacula,
habitatio, aedes, aedificium, aula, atrium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Palatium,
thalamum, coenaculum, triclinium, cella, cubiculum,
cubile, secessus, diversorium, hospitium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid,</HI> 
542. — Hypogaeum, solarium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  543.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Repositoria.</HI>  — Sacrarium, donaria, Isidorus, LXXXII,
545. — Aerarium, armarium, bibliotheca, promptuarium,
cellarium, apotheca,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  546.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Operaria.</HI>  — Ergasterium, ergastula, gynecaeum, pistrinum,
Isidorus, LXXXII, 546. — Clibanus seu clivanus,
furnus, torcular, calcatorium, lacus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  547.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aditus.</HI>  — Vestibulum, porticus, janua, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 547. — Ostium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Fores, valvae, claustra,
fenestrae, cardo, limina, postes, antae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  548.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Partes aedificiorum.</HI>  — Fundamentum, parietes, parietinae,
Isidorus, LXXXII, 548. — Angulus, culmina, camerae,
laquearia, absida, testudo, arcus, pavimenta, ostracus,
compluvium, tepellae, bases,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  549. — Columnae,
capitella, epistylia, tegulae, lateres, canalis, fistulae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid,</HI> 
550. — Munitiones,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Munitum, vel munimentum,
cors seu chors, vallum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Agger, maceriae, formatum
sive formatium, saepes, caulae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  551.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Tentoria.</HI>  — Tentoria, tabernacula, papiliones, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 551.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aedificia rustica.</HI>  — Capanna ( <HI REND="ITALIC">cabane</HI> ) tesqua, magalia,
Isidorus, LXXXII, 552.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fornaces fabrorum.</HI>  — Ignis, fabrica, flamma, fornax,
caminus, carbo, favilla, pruna, Isidorus, LXXXII, 670,
671.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fabrorum instrumenta.</HI>  — Incus, malleus, marcus, marculus,
martellus, forcipes, lima, coelum, Isidorus, LXXXII,
671.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fabrica parietum.</HI>  — Architectae, machiones, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 672.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Dispositio aedificiorum.</HI>  — Isidorus, LXXXII, 672.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Constructio aedificiorum.</HI>  — Constructio, structio, aedificatio,
instauratio, fundamentum, caementum, lapides,
Isidorus, LXXXII, 672.</P> <P COM="0585">Variae species lapidum. — Albus, tiburtinus, tophus,
arenatius, gaditanus, piperinus, conchleatius, columbinus,
molaris, sphungia, silex, albi, silices, viridis silex,
pallidus silex, globus silex, fluviatilis silex, tegulae seu
imbrices, laterculi, Isidorus, LXXXII, 672, 673.</P> <P COM="0585">Lateres, crates, lutum, calx viva, gypsum, arena, columnae,
ordo doricus, iohicus, tuscanicus, corinthius et
atticus, bases, capitella, epistylia, pavimenta, ostracus,
rudi, canalis, fistulae, Isidorus, LXXXII, 675.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Venustas aedificiorum.</HI>  — De laqueariis, de frustis, de
lithostrotis, Isidorus, LXXXII, 675. — De plastis, de
pictura, de coloribus, sinopis, rubrica, syricum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
676. — Phoenicum, minium, cinnabaris, prasina, chrysocolla,
cypria, sandaracha, arsenicum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  677. — Ochra,
caeruleum, purpurissum, indicum, atramentum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
678. — Usta, melinum, annulare, cerussa, chaleanthum,
etc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  679.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta aedificiorum.</HI>  — Norma, regula, perpendiculum,
linea, trulla, martellus, machina, scalae, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 680.</P> <P COM="0585"><HI REND="ITALIC">Lignarii.</HI>  — Carpentarius, navicularius, sarcitector, tignarius,
Isidorus, LXXXII, 680. — Lignum, materia, trabes,
tholus, cuplae, luctantes, agrant seu atlantes, asseres,
scindulae, epigri, clavi, tabulae, commissura,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
681. — Sectio, serra, circinus, securis, bipennis, dolabra
dextralis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  682. — Ascia, asciola, scalpus, scalpellus,
tenebra, taratrum, scofina, cantherium, galla, guvia,
etc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid,,</HI>  683. — De aedificiis publicis, Rabanus Maurus,
III, 375. — De portis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  385. — De viis, de plateis,
de cloacis, de foro,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  386. — De curia, de praetorio,
de gymnasio, de capitolio, de arcibus, de amphitheatro,
de labyrinthis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  387. — De pharo, de thermis,
de tabernis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  388. — De macello, de carcere,
de habitaculis, CXI, 389. — De aedificiis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  391. — De
aditibus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  398. — De parietibus aedificiorum,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid,</HI>  400. — De depositariis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  405. — De officinis,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De munitionibus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  406. — De tentoriis,
 <COL N="0586"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  408. — De sepulcris,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De aedificiis rusticis,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  409. — De fabricis parietum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  559. — De dispositione
aedificiorum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De constructione,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
560. — De venustate aedificiorum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  562. — De laqueariis,
de crustis, de lithostrotis, de plastis, de pictura,
de coloribus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  563. — De instrumentis aedificiorum,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  564. — De lignariis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  565. — Descriptio
domus Salomonis, Petrus Comestor, CXCVIII, 1367,
1368.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Altaria.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Altaria Christianorum.</HI>  — Altarium ornatus, S. Paulinus,
Notanus episc., LXI, 467; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 545. — De
aris beatae Mariae et duodecim apostolis dedicatis,
S. Aldhelmus, LXXXI, 291. — De restauratione monasterii
Centulensis, S. Angilbertus, Centul. abbas, XCIV, 842  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI></P> <P COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Arae ethnicorum.</HI>  — Arae deorum, Tertullianus, I, 347
 <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Tituli eorum quibus dedicabantur aris inscripti,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  347. — Ara Victoriae, S. Ambrosius, XVI, 972. — Ara
victoriae, Symmachus, XVIII, 390  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI></P> <P COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Altaris vestes.</HI>  — Linum adhiberi solum debet in sacrificio,
S. Damasus, papa, VIII, 802; S. Aldhelmus,
LXXXIX, 290.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Amae amulae. (Gallice burettes).</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">De amis et amulis, S. Damasus papa, VIII, 801  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI></P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Amphitheatrum.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">In aditu amphitheatri, plura eduliorum genera emebantur,
Tertullianus. I, 493. — Acta SS. Martyrum Perpetuae
et Felicitatis, Anonymus, III, 50. — Descriptio Amphitheatri,
Arnobius, V, 875. — Amphitheatrum Titi, Cassiodorus,
LXIX, 675, 676. — Amphitheatrum in genere,
S. Isidorus, LXXXIX, 539, 659. — De ludo equestri,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
659. — De retiariis, de secutoribus, de laqueariis, de velitibus,
de ferali certamine,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  660. — De ludis circensibus,
de circis, de aurigis, Rabanus Maurus, CXI,
550. — De curru, de equis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  551. — De septem
spatiis, CXI, 552, de equitibus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De peditibus, de
coloribus equorum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  552. — De theatro, de ferali
certamine,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  553.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Annuli.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">Annulus pronubus, Tertullianus, I, 302. — Maritalis
annulus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  685. — Annuli ex ferro fiebant,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid,</HI> 
1310. — Annuli aestivales leviores, hiemales graviores, X,
304. — Annuli Romanorum post Cannensem cladem modio
metiebantur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  485. — Annulis, Isidorus, LXXXII,
701. — Ungulus, Samothracius, thynnius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  LXXXII,
702; B. Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 582.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Aquaeductus.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">De aquaeductu reficiendo, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 629.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Architectae.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">De architectis, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 718. — Lignarii,
carpentarius, navicularius, sarcitector, tignarius, Isidorus,
LXXXII, 680.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Arma.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">Aries, machina bellica, Tertullianus, II, 1031. — Aries
a Carthagin. inventa,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  1032. — Clypei Persarum
imagine solis adornati erant, id., I, 370. — Descriptio armorum
Francorum, Sidonius Apollinaris, LVIII, 666. — De
armorum factoribus, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 720. — De
signis, aquilae, S. Isidorus LXXXII, 642. — Dracones, pilae,
vexillum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  643. — Buccina, tuba,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Classica,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  644. — De armis proprie dictis, gladius, acies,
capulus, mucro, machaera, framaea, spatha, semispathium,
pugio, clunabulum, chelidoniacus, sica, secures, franciscae,
hasta, contus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  644, 645. — Trudes, venabula,
lancea, amentum, clava, catya, phalarica, pila,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
646. — Telum, cuspis, sagitta, scaptor, spicula, scorpio,
pharetra, cariti, vagina, theca, dolones,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  647. — Arcus,
funda, balista, aries, pluteus, musculus, clypeus,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  648. — Scutum, umbo, ancile, pelta, cetra, parma,
lorica, squama, cassis, galea, apex,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  649. — De
instrumentis bellicis, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 535. — De
buccinis et tubis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De armis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  536. — De
gladiis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De hastis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  539. — De sagittis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — De
pharetris,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  540. — De fundis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  541. — De
ariete, de clypeis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  542. — De loricis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  543. — De
galeis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  544.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Babel.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">Babyloniorum turris superbissima, Tertullianus, II,
174; Sulpicius Severus, XX, 97.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0586" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0586"><HI REND="ITALIC">Balnea, thermae.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0586">Thermae, Balnea, Apodyterium, S. Isidorus, LXXXII,
 <COL N="0587"></COL> 540. — Balneum Baianum, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 560, 771. — De
apodyterio, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 388.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0587" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0587"><HI REND="ITALIC">Baptisterium.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0587">Ex libello de munificentia Constantini, Constantinus
Magnus, VIII, 804. — Descriptio Baptisterii, in quo baptizatus
est Constantinus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Baptisterium S. Agnetis,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  808; S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 545. — Baptisterium
Moguntiae, Venantius Fortunatus, LXXXVIII, 105; Liber
decimus Romanorum Pontificum, CV, 94.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0587" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0587"><HI REND="ITALIC">Basilica, ecclesia.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0587">Ecclesia juxta Thermas Trajanas, Romae, S. Damasus
papa, ex libro Pontificali, VIII, 800. — Basilica Constantiana,
ex libro  <HI REND="ITALIC">De munificentia Constantini,</HI>  VIII, 803. — Basilica
