argentum, plumbum, stangnum (stannum), cuprum, messing,
ferrum, chalybs, S. Hildegardis, CXCVII, 1347-1350.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0588" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0588"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fontes.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="0589"></COL> <P COM="0589">Jubet Theodoricus Aponem fontem refici, Cassiodorus,
LXIX, 568. — Fontis Arethusae descriptio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  762. — Fontis
Marciliani descriptio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  765.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fornaces fabrorum.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Ignis, fabrica, flamma, fornax, caminus, favilla, pruna,
S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 670. — Carbo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  671. — Instrumenta
fabrorum, incus, malleus, marcus, marculus, martellus,
forcipes, lima, coelum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 558.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Gemmaria ars.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">De cultu femin., Tertullianus, I, 1311. — Maris Britannici
et Indici conchiae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Lapides insigniores, B. Rabanus
Maurus, CXI, 463. — Gemmae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  464  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — De
margaritis, de crystallis, de vitro,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  472, 474. — Liber
lapidum, Marbodus, episc. Rhedonensis, CLXXI, 1737,
1738.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Habitacula.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Habitatio, aedes, aedificium, aula, atrium, S. Isidorus,
LXXXII, 541. — Palatium, thalamum, coenaculum, triclinium,
cella, cubiculum, cubile, secessus, diversorium,
hospitium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  542. — Popina, tabernae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  540.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Horologium.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Horologium aquatile et solare, Cassiodorus, LXIX, 539.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.;</HI>  541,  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.;</HI>  Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 610.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Idola.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Artes omnes olim ad idolorum fabricationem aut cultum
spectabant, Tertullianus, I, 668,  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Artifices ex
Etruria Romani arcessivere, id., II, 1050. Asinos adorabant
ethnici cum Epona et Iside, id., I, 557. — Asini caput
et effigiem adoravisse Christiani quam falso accusati,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
364. — Tacitus dedit huic calumniae occasionem,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
364. — Quanta impudentia nebulo Judaeus ridiculam ejus
picturam cum hac inscriptione: DEUS CHRISTIANORUM ONOCHOETES,
circumtulerit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  372  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  579. — Phidias Jovem
Olympium sculpsit, id., II, 803. — Simulacra a Tuscis inventa,
id., I, 430. — Fiebant ex terrena ac vili materia,
et vasculis communi ac vilissimo usui destinatis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  399
 <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Metallis censentur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  341. — Nulla deorum simulacra
apud Romanos,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  430, et 608. — Sive ante Numam
Pompilium  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Antequam ad hominis effigiem efficta
sint, quam ridicula fuerint,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  339, 366, 578. — Esse
deos hujusmodi putabant gentiles,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  488, 579. — Ac
deos fieri ridicula consecratione,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  339  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Sine
capite sunt aliquando,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.</HI>  — Cruci ac stipiti superstruuntur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  340, 579. — Asciis dolantur, runcinis et scabinis
perpoliuntur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  579. — Inquinata, violata, fracta,
minuta, destructa, consumpta,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  344. — A milvis,
muribus et araneis coinquinata,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  343. — Ea ut fierent
pendebat ex imperatorum arbitrio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  439. — Eorum
fatum mutabant artifices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  339  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Ea in aliam formam
convertebant, pignorabant et vendebant,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  344. — Eo
charius vendita quo sanctior Deus, id., II, 346, 576. — Illa
quilibet eligere aut repudiare poterat, id, 344 — De
vanitate idolorum, S. Cyprianus V, 563-564. — Deorum
fabricatio depingitur, Minucius Felix, III, 311, 312. — Simulacrorum
fabricatio, Arnobius, V, 767. — Deorum formae
ridiculae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI>  1213, 1214. — Ridiculae deorum dearumque
statuae, Lactantius, VI, 226  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.</HI>  — Statua Veneris
S. Zeno, episc. Veron., XI, 195, 296- 305. — De errore
profanarum religionum, Julius Firmicus Maternus, XII,
981, 982. — Aurelius Prudentius, LX, 117, 118. — De
scriptio simulacri Serapidis, Saturni ac Canopi, Rufinus,
presbyter Aquileiensis, XXI, 529, 540, 534  <HI REND="ITALIC">seq.;</HI>  S. Augustinus,
XLI, 184. — De statua aenea Comensi, Cassiodorus,
LXIX, 566.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta architectarum.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Norma, regula, perpendiculum, linea, trullae, martellus,
machina, scalae, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 680. — De instrumentis
aedificiorum, Rabanus Maurus, CXI, 564.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Instrumenta fabrorum.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Incus, malleus, marcus, marculus, martellus, forcipes,
lima, coelum, S. Isidorus, LXXXII, 671.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0589" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0589"><HI REND="ITALIC">Libri.</HI></HEAD> <P COM="0589">Bibliothecarum exercitatio, Tertullianus, I, 610. — Bibliotheca
Pisistrati ac Ptolemaei Philadelphi,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ibid.,</HI> 
379. — Bibliothecae apud Serapaeum Ptolemaei, cum ipsis
