quo differat a chao poetae, 1156 not. Troglodytae ita dicti
a  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trwvgh</FOREIGN>  sive  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trwvglh</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">latebra</HI>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>duvo</FOREIGN>  subeo, 1126 not. Tropitae
a verbo  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trevpw</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vertere,</HI>  1184.</P> <P COM="0656"><HI REND="ITALIC">Latinitas Philastriana.</HI>  — Alligaturae quid, 1132. Gaudentius
dixit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Suballigaturae</HI>  serm. 4. Bellum a Graeco
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bevloû</FOREIGN>  dicitur quod et a Belo qui prior telo usus est derivatur,
1134 not. Beluinus, 1250. Apud Gellium et Ambrosium.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Capaciter,</HI>  id est, sensu atque visu eum percipiente,
1185. Carra, sive Carrus, plaustri Gallici genus,
1125. Christianitas, 1228, 1249. Circuitores, circumcelliones
