 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Krokovdeiloû</FOREIGN>  a  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Krovkoû</FOREIGN>  crocus, et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>deiliva</FOREIGN> , timor, vel metuens,
430. Daemon, nomine Satanas, designatus, 323.
Diaconus, 475.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Elix</FOREIGN>  seu palmes, et fig. tutor ligneus,
juxta tenerum arborem plantatus ad ipsam firmandam,
305. Haeresis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiåresiû</FOREIGN> , id est electio, secta ab  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiJrevw</FOREIGN> ,
eligere, detrahere, 375, 477.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Gevneion</FOREIGN> , quomodo sit intelligendum,
61, 62  <HI REND="ITALIC">praef.</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Katabolhú kovsmou</FOREIGN>  id est constitutio
mundi, 563.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kathvghthû</FOREIGN>  sive praeceptor, 93.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Lebhton</FOREIGN> 
sive  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>lebeton</FOREIGN>  colobium est sine manicis, 411 not. Martyrion
est ecclesia sive Dei templum, 107. Menologia Graecorum,
quid, 436 not., 455 not.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Olbioû</FOREIGN> , beatus, idem
significat macarius. 116.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Oxuvrugcoû</FOREIGN> , urbs quaedam Aegypti,
408.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pantokravtwr</FOREIGN> , id est omnipotens, 344.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Periú ajrcwðn</FOREIGN> 
cujusdam operis Origenis titulus, id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">De principiis,</HI> 
71, 127; Latine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Periarchon</HI>  scribitur idem opus, 127;
hos Origenis libros partim transtulit Latino sermone
Rufinus, 124.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Poaú</FOREIGN>  sic dicitur herba qua utuntur fullones,
369 not. Presbyter, id est, sacerdos, a  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>presbuvthû</FOREIGN> 
senex. Symbolum, id est, indicium et collatio, 337.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Schðma</FOREIGN> 
id est habitus. duplex distinguitur apud Graecos, scilicet
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú mivkron</FOREIGN> , id est minor, qui erat novitiorum, et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú mevgalon</FOREIGN> 
et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajggevlikon</FOREIGN> , qui virorum erat probatissimorum,
466 not. Typus tertianus, scilicet febris tertiana, 393
not.</P> <P COM="0668"><HI REND="ITALIC">Latinitas.</HI>  — Ablativi pro accusativis usurpati in articulis
symboli, 339 not. Agricola terrae suae, quis, 322.
Amictus; eo nomine dantur vestimenta quae exterius
tegunt, 306. Apostoli agricolae dicuntur, 322; Item venatores,
317. Aratrum verbi Dei. 322. Calcaneum mordere
quis dicatur, 323. Campus animae, in rure animae, 322.
Colles aeterni, mystice quid sint, 332. Deliciae in vilibus,
399. Dentes super lac candidi, 306, 307. Dispersi quinam
sint 317. Fons nec fluvius, nec fluvius fons, 345. Frigus
duplex, et temporis et fidei, 362. Hamus Christi, quid,
354. Huic pro nunc, 349. Inimici quousque dicuntur, 302.
Iniquus pro inimicus, juxta Graecum, 370. Insubstantiva
generatio, quid sit, 346. Invitentur pro irritentur, 316.
Leonis vocabuli, acceptiones variae, 321, 322. Leonis
